            <div xml:id="d547">

                <pb facs="0593" n="579" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg579"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.24/2892a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Brazil</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-15T19:00:00-04:00">April 15, 1944—7
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1229. Department’s 1083, April 4. The Munitions Assignments Board has approved
                    the allocation to Brazil of 1,000 reconditioned trucks, one and one-half ton,
                    4x4 cargo, with existing tire equipment. Delivery schedule is: April 100, May
                    200, June 350, July 350.</p>
                <p>It seems prudent to accept this allocation, since immediate pressure for more
                    might prejudice our future position. Ambassador Martins has been informed and
                    will present an additional request in June if shipping has been able to absorb
                    scheduled deliveries.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
